{
  "id": "Milne",
  "status": "active",
  "summary": "Source-faithful Milne frontier. The affine invariant quotient core, stable affine neighborhoods under the exact orbit-in-affine hypothesis, characteristic-free finite-group localization of invariants, invariant basic-open identification, and restricted quotient-map compatibility are verified producers. Global finite quotients, symmetric powers, descent, and the remaining abelian-variety geometry remain downstream milestones.",
  "comments": 0
}
{
  "id": "Milne.affine-quotient",
  "status": "done",
  "summary": "Done in MilneLib/InvariantQuotient.lean: fixed-point integrality, finite projection and finite-type carrier over a noetherian base, surjectivity, quotient topology, orbit fibers, spectrum action, and unique factorization for invariant affine maps. This is a producer, not the global finite-quotient theorem.",
  "comments": 0
}
{
  "id": "Milne.finite-quotient",
  "status": "pending",
  "summary": "Pending source node prop:milne-finite-quotient. Stable opens now descend through the affine quotient with exact pullback; invariant basic opens, binary lattice laws, and a surjective restricted orbit-fiber map are verified in InvariantQuotientOpen.lean. Next identify restricted scheme sections on overlaps, prove canonical transitions and their cocycle, and construct Scheme.GlueData; the arbitrary-target universal property, sheaf quotient, and free-action etaleness remain separate.",
  "comments": 0
}
{
  "id": "Milne.symmetric-power",
  "status": "pending",
  "summary": "Pending source node prop:milne-symmetric-power. The relative-power permutation maps form a composition-verified Aut-valued S_n action, while invariant localization and restricted basic-open quotient compatibility are reusable upstream producers. Still prove the product-action orbit-in-affine premise, global quotient gluing and factorization, and separability; do not infer existence or separability from SymmetricPowerData.",
  "comments": 0
}
{
  "id": "Milne.descent",
  "status": "pending",
  "summary": "Pending source node prop:milne-descent-varieties. Build semilinear affine descent, stable-cover sheaf/gluing data, and effective quasi-projective descent; keep imported or conditional interfaces visibly distinct from proved producers.",
  "comments": 0
}

